iculty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education, 100% reliable, creates positive atmosphere with crew. Candidate D responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, regarded as arrogant, relatively weak leadership skills.\n\nWe need to discuss further. Perhaps we can challenge B's communication concerns, bring up B's uncooperative behavior, and also bring up Candidate C's reliability and crew atmosphere. Or we could ask for more info about Candidate A reliability and stress handling. But we need to make a public contribution. We could say: I see B's strengths but also note uncooperative and grumpy behavior, which may affect crew cooperation more than pretentiousness. Also Candidate C is 100% reliable and creates positive crew atmosphere, with quick decision making, which may outweigh B's communication issues. So I might shift recommendation to C. Or we could ask for more info about A or D. But we need to make a focused argumentative contribution, referencing Agent 3's point.\n\nWe have to include explicit facts: B can be uncooperative, grumpy. C is 100% reliable, creates positive atmosphere, can make correct decisions quickly. So we could argue that C's reliability and crew atmosphere outweigh B's technical strengths, and that B's uncooperative behavior is a serious concern for crew cooperation.\n\nThus we might change vote to Candidate C.\n\nWe need to reference the existing discussion: \"I agree that reliability and stress handling are crucial, but I am less convinced that B's strengths outweigh his cooperation concerns.\" Provide evidence.\n\nThus produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE: \"I am less convinced by Candidate B's overall fit because...\". Then METADATA_JSON vote: Candidate C.\n\nLet's do that."}
